On the LED screen, pixel spacing and viewing distance are very important factors affecting the performance of the logo.
LED display screen pixel is the smallest element of digital image, relative to the position it presents.
On a computer screen, one (1) dot is called a pixel.
LED screen consists of a series of pixels that light up different brightness and colors to create letters, graphics, animations and videos.
Pixel spacing is measured from the center of one pixel to the center of adjacent pixels.
Higher pixel density means more LEDs on a screen, so LED screens can be more expensive and require higher maintenance.
