refers to the brightness of each primary color of LED display screen at the highest gray level and maximum brightness under a certain ambient illumination.
For the outdoor LED display screen, according to the use of the environment, there will be different requirements for the maximum brightness, because in the environment where the light is relatively strong, the brightness of the LED display screen is required to be higher, so that the masses can see clearly the contents displayed on the screen.
The requirements of facing east and West and facing south are the same, because the sunlight will directly shine on the LED display screen for part of the time.
When we see the color of the image on the LED display screen is inconsistent with or different from the material, our picture will be seriously distorted, which is related to the color temperature of the white balance of the LED display screen.
If it is the display screen used by TV station, the actual color temperature of the screen body needs to be adjusted to 5 About 500K, so that the picture on the screen is real after being recorded and broadcast by the camera.
If the refresh rate is too low, the LED display will shake when the human eye looks at it.
Generally, the human eye requires a refresh rate of more than 300Hz, that is, as long as the refresh rate exceeds 300Hz, the LED display screen will not shake when viewed with naked eyes.
High refresh can improve the brightness and color fidelity of the display.
This indicator is particularly important when renting screens and television broadcasts.
Under the indoor dark environment, the human eye looks at the high brightness small spacing LED display screen closely and for a long time.
