Chainlink has the characteristics of a decentralized oracle service project, which is considered to function as a mediator between the blockchain and external systems by acting as a third-party service that provides smart contract services that hold external information.
As such, Chainlink can be viewed as a way to prevent the problem of reliability degradation that can occur when data created outside the blockchain system is entered into a smart contract.
In addition, Chainlink has an advantage in that it can increase security by using a distributed oracle and source system, and accurate and reliable data aggregation is possible through this process.
