Despite issues such as the Mount Cox hack and the infamous Bitcoin hard fork over the past few years, there has been a steady stream of efforts to increase the value of cryptocurrencies.
However, the most important point is that Bitcoin is a public blockchain that provides personal privacy as a store of value, and anyone can see the transactions that occur on the network. For certain people, the fact that this public blockchain exposes individual privacy is a very serious matter.
First of all, in order to upgrade Bitcoin, a vote must be passed unanimously by node users.
Because of this, I tried a few upgrades, but failed every time because I couldn't get a power match. Didn't even try to upgrade.
TapRoot is a soft fork designed to improve Bitcoin's scripts to improve personal privacy and improve transaction-related elements.
However, the upgrade can “cloak” the creation and movement of all Bitcoin transactions.
This does not change the fact that the wallets of the initial sender and the final sender are exposed.
As mentioned above, this upgrade was successful because all node operators have adopted this taproot consensus.
It's getting harder and harder as you get to know it. But since it's an upgraded content, you need to check what it is, right?
Among other vertices, Schnorr signatures are known for being compact and efficient in generating short signatures.
The reason I chose this over the Schnorr signature was that it was already widely used, well-known, and safe open source.
This allows the signatures of multiple subjects involved in a transaction to be “consolidated” into a single Schnorr signature.
Exam questions had to be graded, but with the traditional signature method, 30 individual exam papers had to be scored and signed.
Then, I bundle the test papers of each group and sign 6 times, so it is concise.
2) Higher TPS (Transactions Per Second) increase because more transactions can be processed per block.
This approach can make it appear that the transaction never occurred through a network attack.
Taproot is a Bitcoin upgrade that has received much anticipation and support. Because it is implemented with Schnorr signature, privacy, scalability, security, etc.
This upgrade will also increase interest in the Lightning Network as a whole and encourage multi-signature to become an industry standard.
