What is Skype and how does it work
Through this article, we will be talking about what Skype is about, and how this great and useful communication app works, which is also free.
This is an application of voice over ip, What does this mean? That it has the possibility of working with voice signals through the IP protocol.
However, with the passing of command to Microsoft, Skype has not stopped improving its functions and services, in order to remain one of the best free communication applications in the world.
This application makes use of the P2P technology, which allows it to be a very flexible application, also gives it sound quality and fluidity in calls.
To allow direct voice communications between your users,the Skype application uses an Internet protocol of the voice over IP type, also called VozIP or VoIP, which makes it possible for voice signals to be transformed into digital packets that are sent over the Internet.
Live call recording and subtitles.
These are many of the functions that Skype brings, and that undoubtedly makes it one of the most used communication applications. Related Posts
