This kind of inseparable is one of the best options little birds to have at home and tame. In addition, in a short time they let themselves be caught by their caregivers.
Many of the people who have had these palove hearts they claim that once two lovebirds get together as a couple, they will be faithful to each other; and in case one of them dies, the other will never be reunited with another parakeet. In some cases, even to the extent that he may die shortly after his partner died.
The Rosy-faced lovebird originated and distributed in southwestern Africa; specifically encompassing the desert of Namibia, southwestern Angola, and occupying part of the warm places, savannas, dry areas, forest trees, preferably close to water.
Its weight is around 50 gr and its height is 15 cm long; usually the female is slightly larger.
El sound emitted by Agapornis Roseicollis It is very particular and it is something characteristic of them; They spend most of all singing, whistling, and making happy sounds every time I provoke them during the day.
It has a plumage with bright emerald green tones in most of the body, with the lower part lighter and the wings somewhat darker. While some have a salmon pink color on the head, others have a mostly intense red.
As for the white ring that borders its eyes, it tends to be finer than the rest of the lovebirds with a brown iris. The sharp bill is off-white; the legs are greyish in color and are accompanied by fine as well as tiny dark gray nails.
Color and ccharacteristics of the female Roseicollis
As to color of the female pink-faced Inseparable, It is usually paler than the male, although its difference is not so noticeable because it has the same colors in each part of its body, only that the female is more opaque.
All Roseicollis males they are smaller and thinner than females.
It also has a bright blue tail and green colors in the rest of the feathers that accompany its body. At its base there is a black color with orange and red outlining the end.
There are also a variety of color mutations in this species, which have been selectively bred.
When we talk about mutations in the Roseicollis group, we have almost all the colors that we can imagine: oranges, yellows, cinnamon, violet, turquoise, among others.
So that you can get these little green birds with orange face, parents must have an orange face or be carriers.
In this a dominant mutation occurs, in which birds with darker colors. They are usually named with a letter "D" when we only have a chromosome with dark factor and DD, when we have both.
The rest of her face has a slight, rather pale shade of pink. The beak, legs, and nails maintain their original color.
What is particular about this mutation is that the birds are left with almost all blue bodies, accompanied by a turquoise tone on their wings and contrasted by green feathers.
The legs in this mutation are brown, the tail or shirt is brown instead of being black, as it naturally usually is.
In this mutation, our birds have a light yellowish green color on their body; the rump becomes light blue. Legs, nails and beak gray like concrete.
All little parakeets they are yellow in color all over their body; his mask is red, the rump and back are white; their eyes turn red and their legs light pink.
In this opportunity we will have pastel green birds, the T-shirt acquires a fairly light gray tone, the rump turns bluish, the mask is reddish, and finally the legs and nails are very light pink.
Opaline parakeets they are striking green with gray, their rump is green. Scarlet mask and head, its nape has a light pink color.
In this mutation, the birds are amber in color with emerald flashes, accompanied by red eyes and flesh-colored legs. Roseicollis dilute
Birds with a harlequin mutation have the peculiarity that their coloration in the plumage is not uniform. You have certain spots on your body.
It is a fairly intelligent parrot, many of this species have learned to do tricks and other things.
How are Roseicollis lovebirds in freedom
It is advisable not to house another species with these birds, because when the females are in heat or have nests, they tend to be aggressive and territorial.
These birds have the characteristic of preferring hot places. Therefore, the ideal place to place the cage of a Pink-faced Inseparable, It is in a fairly warm environment, in which the temperature is around 20-25˚C at least.
We can place it outside the house, as long as there is not much breeze, or in an area that is not near the air conditioners of the house.
Equally the size or measure of the cage will depend on the amount of lovebirds that we want to have at home.
The cage must be at least 40cm wide x 40cm long and 60cm high. The distance between the grid or the spacing between the metal bars should be 1 cm maximum, so that our little birds do not get stuck or come out.
Must have about feeders or containers for bird food. There are cages that already come with this integrated, and if not, we must buy them.
A handle in the upper part in case we want to transport our cage.
Several horizontal bars or hangers, which can be made of wood or resistant plastic; so that they serve as rest, and so that our parakeets can stand.
Some Toys to keep parakeets entertained, such as: bells, swings, mirrors, stairs. It is important that it be made of a special material for this type of bird since any other can damage its beak.
All these tips will guarantee the quality of life of our little parakeets, and also the comfort when reproducing.
This should preferably be made of wood, with a circular hole in the front, it should be large enough so that it can enter and exit without any difficulty.
How big should the nest be for these little birds?
Another important fact to keep in mind is that our parakeets must be at least 10 months old and from this time to many years they will be reproducing.
In the breeding season, their behavior is usually different. The female will concentrate on preparing the nest, we will help her by offering her fine twigs, palm branches, dry leaves and paper, which they love because many strips make it.
At the time of laying, the female lays between three and six eggs that will take about 20 or 25 days to hatch. Then the birds will take a couple of weeks, or more than a month to leave the nest; You will only notice its small head poking out, and the mother protecting them.
Care so that lovebirds last for many years
Supply of calcium, which will help the chicks to form well when the female lays her eggs.
Provide them with an ideal vitamin complex for lovebirds, composed of vitamins A, D3 and E, which help to increase fertility.
Just as there are vitamins, there are also supplements for the prevention of parasites. The truth is that all these supplements and vitamins will help to have a healthier life, since our parakeets last for many years.
In addition to this, supplement it with a diet rich in calcium, that is, that the foods we give it have this nutrient among its components.
All food for parakeets they must be fresh, and the seeds must be of quality. Also, add vitamins and supplements.
There are many supplements and vitamins that are beneficial for our birds, and among them we have:
Skin supplements of the lovebirds, in case you have any wound it will help you heal quickly.
You can not miss the most used in our parakeets, such as the football. It should be given every time it is in the breeding season, or when it is lacking in calcium.
Other ideal vitamins for little birds are those that contain zinc, iodine or magnesium, highly recommended during the breeding season.
Clean their eyes and feathers constantly.
Be on the lookout if you lose a lot of feathers or if you don't have an appetite.
We must keep their cage and nest clean to avoid fungi and bacteria.
When they are in the chick stage they will eat porridge, which will be their food when they leave the nest. It is important to give them enough so that they are well fed.
We can buy the porridge in the pet store and simply prepare it by placing a little hot water and adding the porridge. This should not be too thick or too liquid, we must mix well so that there are no lumps.
We can also prepare the porridge, called “homemade porridge”, the most common is the one prepared based on oatmeal, rice and egg flours; of the latter it is preferable to use only the yolk.
