The Masked Inseparable or Blackheaded They are a species of Psittaciform Birds of the Psittaculidae Native to the Northeast region of Tanzania and Kenya, it is commonly bred in captivity as a pet.
This little bird it is one of the most prominent among members of its species. He is cheerful, sociable, vigorous, gentle and generally one of the calmest of the group of inseparable ones.
His song is wonderful; they have an easy-to-recognize chip-chip, their tune is high, and they can even learn some words. Listen to birdie, It brings satisfaction to the owner, while indicating that he is happy with his home.
Other Species Names Personatus (personata) Thanks to its distinguished physique, mainly due to its blackened head, it has been nicknamed the masked lovebird, inseparable black-headed or in English Masked lovebird, inseparable black-headed.
Although many people may not believe it, parrots masked They have their origin in East Africa; specifically it was discovered during the XNUMXth century in northern Tanzania.
Even thanks to this delimitation, both species have crossed, resulting in new hybrids capable of procreating; Parrots appear similar to the Fischers but with darker heads.
They are one of the smallest of the members of their family, both in weight and height. Measuring a mere 14 or 15 cm and weighing a maximum of 55 grams and a minimum of 45 grams.
All inseparable Personata They are very clever and spirited, so their singing could not be far from it. They have a melodious and high voice that for some is classified as an incessant screech or whistle.
They enjoy daily baths and drying their fluffy feathers in the sun, but they also love chewing on the bars of the cage among other objects.
Remembering that we will only find the ancestral version free, since mutations and so on are the product of mixtures in captivity.
First of all, take into account that even if they are little birds normally calm and domestic, that does not diminish how territorial they can become if they are forcibly included with other birds that are not to your liking.
You have to be very careful about the cage, it cannot be left open for any reason because although some apply the “he loves me very much, and here I give him everything he needs. It will not go away ”, we are talking about animals that are born with an instinct, that of freedom.
Try to leave enough water in the cage so that he drinks and also can take his baths frequently. In general, they do not require as much care as other more sensitive parrots.
It has a plumage of three different and well differentiated colors. Firstly, its characteristic head that shows off the black color, with which the white line located at the base of its reddish and curved bill contrasts.
The soft feathery hood progresses down the neck, fading into the vivacious yellow color of the chest, which is followed by a light green, or Carthusian in the middle and belly.
They also have a hard time trusting the owner, it could even take a year to develop the relationship with the caregiver. That is why patience is the key in raising lovebirds.
Since it is physically difficult to determine whether we are in front of a male or a female with the naked eye, it is said that they have more closed pelvic bones than females. Besides, it is said that his eye ring is thinner.
One way to know if we are dealing with a pigeon or an adult is by the tonality of the plumage, which in the little ones is more opaque.
This has happened thanks to the fact that pigments such as pscitacin and eumelanin have been reduced or modified, so that the feathers change from their ancestral or original color, to a new one.
In its original model, the silky plumage is emerald green or clover, along with the yellow and black located on its head. They have a gleaming red beak and perfectly drawn white around their eyes.
What he keeps is the black mask on his face, and the white eye ring. Without a doubt it is one of the most requested mutations because of how beautiful the birds resulting.
