Minecraft it is a sensational game in which we can play even in local area networks (lan) with our family or friends, however, it is not funny when the Lan world does not appear, but calm down I am here to explain Why does the world Lan not appear in Minecraft?
The reasons why the Lan world does not appear in Minecraft There are many, so identifying our problem usually takes a long process, so I will show you which are the most common of these, and how to solve each of them.
Go to "Control Panel" on your PC.
Now "Windows firewall".
Click on the "Change settings" icon indicating what you want to do. "Administrative changes".
With this simple change you should no longer have a problem connecting with the Lan World of Minecraft.
If they are all connected to the same network, but still cannot connect, this could be due to a feature on your router called “AP isolation”. To check if everything is fine, you just need to do a ping test on your computers and for this you just have to:
Go up a bit and write down the "IPv4 address" of all computers, and check if they can communicate with each other over the network with the remote "Ping".
Now if the computers failed their "Ping" then most likely they have a problem with the "AP isolation" To solve this you will have to consult the documentation of your specific router to see where the configuration is and deactivate it, after deactivating it the problem in question will be solved.
To solve this just make sure all computers are connected on the same network. It is often the case that laptops are connected to a open Wi-Fi network or nearby that you have used previously and let's not notice, if that's the case, let's just make sure that all the computers are connected to the same local network with the same name and that's it, problem solved.
If none of these options solved the problem, it is likely that the problem itself, is that the game of Minecraft for some reason I am not polling the network or updating the list of Lan games available correctly.
