It has options in SD, HD and UHD video quality (Standard, High definition and Ultra high definition) available. Because of this data consumption used per hour may vary when viewing your favorite content.
Netflix allows content streaming through three video options: Low, Medium and High quality. The low and medium quality options offer content in standard definition, while the high definition option could transmit in HD and UHD.
Data consumption on Netflix is calculated according to video quality, which is why it is as follows:
How to control data consumption with Netflix
Don't worry, Netflix offers options with which you can support yourself to have a good data management from the application.
The option Save Data in the Netflix app limits data usage to approximately 6 hours of viewing per 1 GB of data usage. Streaming quality is low, but more durable per GB.
then in Cellular data usage.
