For players of Minecraft It has become a fever to create their own houses, they have come to create large and luxurious structures, of course, when we are starting we do not have the slightest idea of how to achieve our mission, although it seems something very complicated once you have the least notion It becomes very simple, therefore, we will leave you the following steps to make your own home.
The safest thing is that if we do not know how to build a house in the world of Minecraft We have to start from the simplest, in order to gradually create something more complicated. Create houses in Minecraft in the 'creative mode' and 'survival mode' is practically the same, the only difference is that in the 'survival mode' we will have to look for our materials, while in the 'creative mode' we will have them on hand.
The second step is to select the location where we will build our house; a good proposal would be somewhere close to a village, this will serve to make deals or barter with the villagers and so we can supply ourselves. Water supplies must always be taken into account, that is, the place must be carefully evaluated as water is important if you want to build a house.
The third step is to choose our materials (this is essential), among which we can use, we have: Wood (wooden planks), brick and stone, for our walls. Wood is the easiest material to get, but brick and stone are more resistant, it will be up to each one to use the material they like the most.
Now that we have the foundation of our house (the walls) we will place the windows and the door. Then we will place the roof, in the 'creative mode' we can do it from inside the house, pressing twice the 'space bar', in the case of him 'survival mode' We will place it from the inside, pointing with the mouse upwards where we will start the construction of the roof.
We must also place lighting, an option could be to place torches, but it is not recommended in wooden houses since they could catch fire (it would be devastating); the other items that could be placed are a bed, our 'craft table', Our 'sharpening stone' and any decorative element.
